  "description": "The narrowing at app/cbl/COMEN01C.cbl:187 - MOVE WS-MESSAGE TO ERRMSGO OF COMEN1AO - sending PIC X(80) from line 38 into the PIC X(78) of app/cpy-bms/COMEN01.CPY:138. A COBOL alphanumeric MOVE fills the receiver from the LEFT and discards the overflow, so the surviving text is the LEADING seventy-eight characters and the trailing two bytes are lost; a receiver filled from the right would shift every character two places and is what the direction assertion rules out. The invalid-key text is used because at fifty characters it distinguishes the two directions, where an all-space message could not. Driven through the controller because the service produces the eighty-byte working-storage field and only the controller produces the seventy-eight-byte screen field, and the two travel on separate message channels for exactly that reason.",
